Subject: [PATCH] Reject a leading dash in an implicit CVS root
Origin: https://src.opensuse.org/pool/cvs/src/branch/factory/cvs-Bug-1053364-disallow-dash.patch
CVE: CVE-2017-12836

Prevent a CVS root beginning with a dash from being interpreted as an
option by a program invoked by CVS.
---
diff --git a/src/root.c b/src/root.c
--- a/src/root.c
+++ b/src/root.c
@@ -619,0 +620,13 @@ parse_cvsroot (const char *root_in)
+    else if (*cvsroot_copy == '-')
+    {
+        /* Without an explicit method, the root may begin with a user name,
+           host name, or path.  None needs a leading dash: relative paths can
+           use "./".  Reject it so that a crafted root cannot become an
+           option to a program invoked by CVS.  */
+        error (
+            0,
+            0,
+            "CVSROOT (`%s') must not start with a dash.",
+            cvsroot_copy);
+        goto error_exit;
+    }
